INT. ABANDONED CAROUSEL - FAIRGROUND - NIGHT

A circus-striped dome, peeling. Painted horses frozen mid-gallop, manes cracked. Mirrors fogged. Moonlight in knife blades through torn canvas. Pigeons. Cold.

AGENT TAMSIN REEVES, 30s, tactical vest, hair tied back, stands at the center pole with a pistol low and a phone in her other hand. Her breath smokes. Her eyes never stop moving.

ODALYS KANE (V.O.)
(phone, calm)
Take one more step toward the horses.

TAMSIN
I'm at the pole.

ODALYS KANE (V.O.)
Take it anyway.

She steps. The floor creaks like a ship.

TAMSIN
Where are you?

ODALYS KANE (V.O.)
Where I always am. Behind you.

Tamsin spins. Nothing but mirrors. Her own face, multiplied.

TAMSIN
I don't see you.

ODALYS KANE (V.O.)
No. You see you.

The carousel groans. Slowly, the platform begins to turn. Painted horses rise and fall. Calliope notes wheeze out of dead pipes.

TAMSIN
(into the phone)
Odalys, let her go.

ODALYS KANE (V.O.)
She isn't mine to let go. She's yours.

Tamsin freezes. Between two horses ahead, a small girl in a yellow raincoat, hands bound, watches her. A white dress under the coat. She's very still.

TAMSIN
(whisper)
Mara.

ODALYS KANE (V.O.)
Count the horses, Agent.

TAMSIN
What?

ODALYS KANE (V.O.)
Count them.

Tamsin counts under her breath. Twelve, thirteen, fourteen. She stops.

TAMSIN
There are fifteen horses on the platform.

ODALYS KANE (V.O.)
And one of them is breathing.

Tamsin lifts the pistol. Turns slowly toward the horse nearest the girl, the white one, its painted eyes wide. It shudders. It inhales.

The platform spins faster. The music climbs. She raises the pistol to her shoulder, finger tightening.
